  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "Visit",
    "file": "arrow/cpp/src/arrow/array/util.cc",
    "description": "In ArrayDataEndianSwapper::Visit(const MonthDayNanoIntervalType&), the code iterates using data_->length and reads MonthDayNanos elements from data_->buffers[1] without validating that the buffer is large enough for that many elements. For malformed IPC dictionary data, length can exceed buffer_size/sizeof(MonthDayNanos), causing out-of-bounds read (ASan global-buffer-overflow) at util.cc:210 during endian swapping.",
    "conditions": "The IPC stream must drive dictionary decoding with endian swapping enabled (non-native schema endianness + ensure_native_endian), and provide a dictionary array of MonthDayNanoIntervalType where ArrayData.length is inconsistent with the actual value buffer size (too small). Data flow: fuzz input -> ipc::ReadDictionary(reader.cc) -> internal::SwapEndianArrayData(util.cc) -> ArrayDataEndianSwapper::Visit(MonthDayNanoIntervalType), which trusts length and overreads buffer."
  },
